  "notes": "**From the first bench tests.** Changes found while testing an IC-9700 and an ID-52 PLUS on simplex.\n\n- **Chat: type any call sign in To.** To used to list only stations already heard, so you couldn't address a station before it had transmitted. Now you can type any call sign; heard stations are suggested, and an empty field sends to everyone (CQCQCQ).\n- **Chat: your own call sign in red italics** on the lines you sent, so they stand out from received lines.\n- **Radio test summary shows more:**\n  - a **Received** section: when data arrived and how much;\n  - **channel changes** in the timeline: when the radio reported voice, a signal or a clear channel over CI-V;\n  - plainer port lines, for example `radio UR \"CQCQCQ\" R1 \"W4DOC  D\" R2 \"W4DOC  G\" (read over CI-V)` and \"no air-time limit on this path\".\n\n- **Diagnostics: one Send to the developer button.** It replaces Show file and Upload for the developer: one click highlights the recording in its folder, opens the upload page and copies the file's location. It also appears after Write support bundle.\n\nFirst on-air results: the ID-52 PLUS holds data while it's receiving a D-STAR voice call and sends it when the channel clears. The IC-9700 reports the call signs it's set to, and who it's receiving, over CI-V.",
